From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: ahb: opt into firmware recovery on the AHB path

ath11k_core_ssr_notifier_cb() (core.c:1308) and ath11k_coredump_build()
both call BUG_ON(1) when ab->fw_recovery_support is clear, so any Q6
firmware crash panics the kernel instead of being recovered by SSR.

The flag is only ever assigned in pci.c, and only to false, so no AHB
board can ever have it set - including this one, where the QCN6122 radio
sits on AHB. Set it in the AHB probe path so an SSR event is handled
gracefully: stats are dumped, the radio restarts, and the box stays up.

Observed on the Xiaomi AX3000E (IPQ5018): before this, a firmware
assertion during WiFi bring-up took the whole kernel down.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -959,6 +959,7 @@
 	ab->fw_mode = ATH11K_FIRMWARE_MODE_NORMAL;
 	ab->enable_cold_boot_cal = ath11k_cold_boot_cal;
 	ab->userpd_id = userpd_id;
+	ab->fw_recovery_support = true;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dev_init_lock);
 	left = wait_event_timeout(ath11k_radio_prb_wq, dev_init_progress == false,
